title: 'Starter test: the wget HTTPS-to-HTTP redirect test never exercises a redirect'
updated: 2026-11-18T09:01:23Z
---

Found by the k7 native round-3 review. tests/test_starter.py test_wget_rejects_https_to_http_redirect (about lines 589-635, from 2c972d9) never exercises a redirect: its fake wget writes no server response to stderr, so the starter rejects the download for that reason instead of the HTTPS-to-HTTP redirect. The test still passes with the redirect check in bin/briefing (about line 744) removed.

Done when the fake wget emits a realistic server response that redirects from https to http (the shape real wget prints with -S), the test fails against a starter without the redirect check, and passes with it. The curl path's redirect test should be checked the same way.
